(Bug #79's second half. A number read before its own declaration also
 printed `0` - right by accident, because 0 is what a number defaults to
 and what the zeroed slot holds. Accepting it because the wrong answer
 happens to look correct is how the text case above went unnoticed, so
 this is refused on the same rule and not on the value it produced.)

Print count.
a number called count is 42.
